//!
//! Tracks and manages the op-memory service: persistent knowledge-graph memory
//! backed by Qdrant (semantic vector search over observations) and CozoDB
//! (structured entity/relation graph).
//! Publishes live state to D-Bus under `/opdbus/v1/plugins/memory` so that
//! `register_plugin_projection_tools` can expose it as MCP tools.
//!
//! Schema is grounded in:
//!   - Official MCP memory server (@modelcontextprotocol/server-memory)
//!     tool surface: create_entities, create_relations, add_observations,
//!     delete_entities, delete_observations, delete_relations, read_graph,
//!     search_nodes, open_nodes
//!   - mcp-knowledge-graph (shaneholloman) extended tool surface
//!   - Qdrant REST API — semantic search over entity observations
//!   - CozoDB Datalog API — graph traversal over entity/relation structure
//!
//! Backing infrastructure:
//!   - **Qdrant** — vector store for semantic search over entity observations.
//!     Collection: `memory_observations` (one vector per observation string).
//!     Payload fields: `entity_name`, `entity_type`, `observation`, `context`.
//!   - **CozoDB** — graph store for entity/relation structure.
//!     Relations: `memory_entities[name, entity_type, created_at]`,
//!     `memory_observations[entity_name, observation, created_at]`,
//!     `memory_relations[from_entity, to_entity, relation_type, created_at]`.
//!
//! The canonical schema lives in `memory_schema()` below.

use anyhow::{Context, Result};
use async_trait::async_trait;
use op_state::{
    ApplyResult, Checkpoint, DiffMetadata, PluginCapabilities, StateAction, StateDiff, StatePlugin,
};
use op_state_store::PluginSchema;
